 Changing `nav.astar/v1` to another registered implementation with the same port contract, such as `nav.dijkstra/v1`, changes the algorithm without changing the host program. Removing the smoother and exporting `raw_plan` changes the DAG itself.
 
+## V0 demo
+
+The repository now contains a dependency-free Rust V0 implementation and a runnable navigation planning Quickstart:
+
+```text
+crates/
+  unit-compose-core/        Registry, validation, static DAG, executor, Debug model
+  unit-compose-yaml/        YAML Module Definition frontend
+  unit-compose-debug-html/  Self-contained graph/timing dashboard
+examples/
+  navigation_planning/      Map decoder, inflation, A*/Dijkstra, LOS smoother
+```
+
+Install the pinned Rust toolchain and run all checks:
+
+```bash
+./scripts/bootstrap-rust.sh
+cargo fmt --all -- --check
+cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
+cargo test --workspace
+```
+
+Generate the three shareable demo views:
+
+```bash
+./scripts/demo-all.sh
+```
+
+Then open `target/unit-compose-demo/index.html`. Each page is a single offline HTML file containing the occupancy/cost map, raw and final path, compiled Unit/Resource DAG, execution order, timing, and metrics. No external viewer or CDN is required.
+
+For one configuration:
+
+```bash
+cargo run -p navigation-planning-demo -- \
+  --module examples/navigation_planning/configs/astar.yaml \
+  --start 1.25,1.25 \
+  --goal 9.25,5.75 \
+  --html target/unit-compose-demo/astar.html \
+  --describe
+```
+
+See [the navigation demo guide](examples/navigation_planning/README.md) for implementation boundaries and comparison commands.
+
 ## V0 behavior
 
 V0 deliberately establishes a small, useful baseline:
@@ -77,7 +120,7 @@ V0 deliberately establishes a small, useful baseline:
 - the first Unit error stops further launches and is returned with the Unit identity;
 - Unit private state may persist across runs, but the framework does not roll it back;
 - a Module instance has an immutable DAG; configuration reload builds a new Module and swaps it between runs;
-- Debug can describe the DAG, export DOT or Mermaid, report Resource relationships, and record Unit timing.
+- Debug can describe the DAG, export DOT or Mermaid, report Resource relationships, record Unit timing, and render a self-contained HTML dashboard.
 
 ## Intentionally deferred
 
@@ -85,10 +128,6 @@ The first implementation does **not** require transactional commit or rollback,
 
 These capabilities may be added later through the existing Unit, Resource, Module, and Debug model when representative workloads justify them.
 
